title: You were alone.
new-page: true

No. Not alone.

The junge. That little kid, the cap.

He was there. Hiding, he was crouched to a car. A few feet away. He was stood there, frozen, his fist raised, but meaningless, holy shit, the Boy. 
  
Leo. Your Leo, you felt. It didn’t matter how true it was, he was your son, your only Son, in that moment, at least, he was.

His eyes, they were fixed on you, they were wide, unblinking. Poor boy, poor little boy, no, this will never leave you, will it? My eyes, they'll visit him, forever...Presuming he survived this, if anyone could survive this.

No one could, not unharmed, in some way. 

You wanted to tell him something, something important. You didn’t want to die like this, pathetic, silent. You wanted to say look away, maybe? 
  
Run, run? Remember? Remember my wife who will raise my baby alone? Remember the man with the cart, the women with groceries, remember us, do not let us be in vain? Please, Son, avenge us? Random teenaged child at a political rally, unknowing to the cruel reality of world? Of politics, of power and praise, avenge us?

But no words, if you could think of any, could come out. Warmth was spreading too fast, the world was getting very small. It pulled back at the edges, a photograph curling in a fire. 
  
Fire...Maria’s fireplace, you thought, the memory cam unbidden. The laughing, that gentle tinkle of flame reflected in her eye, her hands ni yours, the faith that, even in a time like that, everything would be okay, because you were together! You were young, the future was endless, wasn't it?

How bitter now it seemed.

The boy stared, the machine gun, everything, it was silent. Was it? No, maybe you couldn't hear it? But you could see, you could see the sky  above Berlin.
  
Pale, indifferent, blue. Linden trees were budding, the hoop, somewhere, you felt, were rolling, rolling, rolling, through empty streets

Leo, you thought, or maybe Maria, little ones, I’m sorry, you thought, I’m sorry I wasn’t there for you, sweet babies, how I wish I could be there.
